370
00:30:47.305 --> 00:30:49.524
ORDER, DUPLICATES AND GAPS IN A CHAT.

371
00:30:49.804 --> 00:31:06.103
2,000 simulated customer↔rider conversations (10 minutes, ~40 messages each) over. mobile networks: requests are lost (5%), acks are lost after the server stored the message (3%, the client retries.

372
00:31:08.953 --> 00:31:09.870
On screen:

373
00:31:10.150 --> 00:31:19.601
2,000 conversations times ~40 messages; 5% request loss, 3% ack loss (retry), heavy-tailed. latency.

374
00:31:19.881 --> 00:31:32.446
5% of pushes dropped, rider clock skew up to ±120 s. design duplicates missing reply before its sender's own msgs. shown message out. of order.

375
00:31:32.726 --> 00:31:41.686
A) no dedupe, sort by sender's clock 2,407 4,034 59,998 0.

376
00:31:41.966 --> 00:31:49.987
B) dedupe by message id, sort by server receive time 0 4,083 0 539.

377
00:31:50.267 --> 00:32:04.070
C) dedupe + per-sender order + conversation seq + gap fetch 0 0 0 0. then phones' clocks can't order a conversation: the rider's replies landed before the. questions they answered.

378
00:32:04.350 --> 00:32:05.865
The rest is in the chapter.

379
00:32:08.715 --> 00:32:09.568
Reading it:

380
00:32:09.848 --> 00:32:11.448
A trusted the sender's clock.

381
00:32:11.728 --> 00:32:20.133
With the rider's clock off by up to two minutes, 59,998 replies were placed before the messages they answered.

382
00:32:20.413 --> 00:32:28.605
Lost ACKs also produced 2,407 duplicates, and dropped pushes 4,034 missing messages.

383
00:32:28.885 --> 00:32:32.427
B used server receive time and deduped by client id.

384
00:32:32.707 --> 00:32:38.488
Causality between people is fixed, because a reply can only be sent after its question was stored.

385
00:32:38.768 --> 00:32:47.728
But the network still reordered 539 of a sender's own rapid messages, and nothing noticed the 4,083 dropped pushes.

386
00:32:49.078 --> 00:32:52.982
C added per-sender order, a conversation sequence and gap fetch:

387
00:32:53.262 --> 00:32:54.713
0 on every measure.

388
00:32:54.993 --> 00:32:58.513
The dropped pushes still happened; phones saw the gaps and fetched.

